  "prefLabel": "Plc 1903.06 Qualifications for Initial State LSP Certification",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1903.06 Qualifications for Initial State LSP Certification. To qualify for initial state LSP certification, an individual shall be:\n\n(a) Certified by the International Board of Certified Lactation Consultant Examiners as an International Board Certified Lactation Consultant (IBCLC);\n\n(b) Certified by the Academy of Lactation Policy and Practice (ALPP) as a certified lactation counselor (CLC);\n\n(c) Certified by the Childbirth and Postpartum Professional Association (CAPPA) as a certified lactation educator (CLE); or\n\n(d) Certified as a certified breastfeeding educator (CBE) by Lactation Education Resources or Childbirth International.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
